    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3840": {
      "title": "Provost and Vice-President (Academic and Research)",
      "description": "Provost and Vice-President (Academic and Research) About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Provost and Vice-President (Academic and Research) (Ref: PV/VPAR 2026-08-03) Responsibilities The Provost and Vice-President (Academic and Research) is a key member of the senior management team and reports to the President.  He/she is primarily responsible for providing academic leadership to all School Deans, and through them, to all academic staff, in ensuring effectiveness and international competitiveness in the conduct of curriculum and programme development, academic quality assurance, student admission, research and academic staffing matters.  He/She will also chair relevant Academic Board (AB) and Senior Management Committee (SMC) Committees as assigned by the President. Reporting to the Provost and Vice-President (Academic and Research) are Deans of Schools, Director of Information Technology, Registrar, University Librarian, and university-level research centres.  More specific duties include: to provide leadership to the overall academic curriculum structure, programme development and quality assurance, in response to the University strategic directions, community needs and changing market situations; to develop research policies and strategies to promote academic and impactful research activities to the community; to oversee the recruitment, assessment, promotion and retention of quality academic staff; to oversee overall student admission policies, strategies and processes; to ensure the smooth management and operations of all academic programmes and matters; to oversee the policies, strategies and operations of continuing and professional education and knowledge exchange for the community; to oversee the development and performance of Schools/Departments/Units under supervision, review and monitoring of their strategic plans, budgets, outputs, efficient and effective use of financial, human and physical resources; to develop, in consultation with Deans and Heads of Departments, an effective performance management system for academic staff, including the setting of performance standards, and continuous staff professional development; and to oversee academic support units and research centres. ​​​​​​​​​​​​​​The Person The ideal candidate should possess the following attributes: academic distinction with an established record of scholarship, teaching and research excellence, and a clear commitment to advancing liberal arts education in conjunction with professional disciplines; a forward-looking academic vision, with the ability to drive high-quality teaching and learning, student success, interdisciplinary development, innovation, and impactful research; proven  leadership experience in academic planning, quality assurance, programme development, faculty development and resource stewardship within a complex higher education environment; strong strategic, analytical and commercial judgement, with the capability to translate institutional priorities into effective policies, initiatives, performance standards and measurable outcomes; strong external engagement capability, supported by international networks and academic standing, to enhance the University’s visibility, strategic partnerships, reputation and influence regionally and globally; and outstanding stakeholder management, communication and relationship-building skills, with the credibility and agility to engage effectively with students, faculty members, staff, Council members, alumni, donors and external partners. .................................................................................................................................................................. Application and Nomination Procedures: Asianet Consultants (H.K.) Limited has been appointed to support this search exercise.  Interested parties are invited to send their applications (which should include a cover letter and a detailed resume) or nominations to Mr. Peter Liu at Unit 05, 29/F, Infinitus Plaza, 199 Des Voeux Road Central, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong, or via hsuhk-pvpar@asianetconsultants.com .  For enquiries, please call (852) 2530 0130. Review of applications and nominations will begin in August 2026 and continue until the position is filled.  The University reserves the right not to fill the position or to fill it by invitation. All information provided will be used solely for the purposes of this search and kept strictly confidential."
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3858": {
      "title": "Department of Supply Chain and Information Management - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Full-time)",
      "description": "Department of Supply Chain and Information Management - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Full-time) About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Department of Supply Chain and Information Management - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Full-time) (Ref: AssoP / AsstP (SCM) 2026-08-21) Responsibilities plan, develop, coordinate and deliver specialist modules; assist in programme development, management and validation; and engage in research, scholarly and administration activities. Applicants Should possess a doctoral degree in a related discipline; have solid teaching and research experience in tertiary education; have a proven track record for scholarly research and publications; possess relevant industry experience preferably; have knowledge of the application of AI tools in teaching and learning; have a high level of subject knowledge, skills and competence in the academic disciplines concerned (especially in Management Science, Supply Chain Management, Transportation, Aviation) ; and have good command of written and spoken English and Chinese preferably. .................................................................................................................................................................. The appointee is expected to assume duty in August 2027 . Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ to apply for the position. Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3850": {
      "title": "Department of Accountancy - Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s)",
      "description": "Department of Accountancy - Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Department of Accountancy - Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Ref: AssoP/AsstP (ACY) 2026-08-14) Responsibilities The Department is searching for highly qualified applicants for positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor ranks. Applicants must have a strong research background and possess a balanced perspective concerning research, teaching and engagement with the accounting profession. The positions are open to all areas of accounting, but special consideration will be given to those with a teaching and research focus in corporate governance and sustainability, taxation and assurance. Applicants Should possess a PhD degree, a professional certification (CPA, CMA etc.) is strongly preferred; have a strong research and publication record; have a proven record of effective and innovative teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels; and preferably have proficiency in data analytics and accounting technologies. .................................................................................................................................................................. The appointee is expected to assume duties in January or August 2027 . Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicants should visit https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and submit an application letter and an up-to-date CV to apply for the position. Review of applications will begin soon and continue until the position is filled. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for a campus visit and asked to provide a job talk paper and three recommendation letters. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only.  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
