    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3863": {
      "title": "Department of Social Science",
      "description": "Department of Social Science - Executive Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 9,900 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Department of Social Science - Executive Officer (Ref: EO (SSC) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities provide support for programme administration and secretarial support for the undergraduate programme, postgraduate programme and the department ; assist in the planning and execution of programme-related activities, including admission exercises, promotion and publicity , assessments and student activities; facilitate the implementation of department-related activities, including seminars, workshops, and conferences; and handle enquiries and liaise with various stakeholders. Applicants Should possess a recognised bachelor’s degree and have at least 3 years of relevant work experience , preferably in the education sector; be proficient in computer skills including Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Chinese w ord p rocessing and management skills in major social media platforms (such as Instagram, Facebook, and WeChat) and website maintenance ; possess good interpersonal and communication skills; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua ); and be a fast learner, a good team player and able to work independently with a strong sense of responsibility. Work experience in the higher education sector will be an advantage. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 27 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3868": {
      "title": "Finance Office - Assistant Manager, Financial Planning",
      "description": "Finance Office - Assistant Manager, Financial Planning About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 9,900 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Finance Office - Assistant Manager, Financial Planning (Ref: AMFP (FO) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities serve as a finance business partner to designated Schools, centres and administrative units, providing timely advice and support on budgeting, financial planning, management reporting and other finance related matters; build strong working relationships with budget holders and stakeholders to understand their operational needs, translate financial information into practical insights, and support informed decision-making; develop and maintain financial models to support feasibility studies, programme planning, knowledge transfer initiatives, self-financing activities and other new opportunities; work closely with cross-functional teams to ensure accurate, timely and user-oriented financial analysis, forecasts and management reports; provide proactive recommendations to improve operational workflows, internal controls, policies, guidelines and financial processes from both Finance Office and user-department perspectives; prepare monthly and quarterly financial and management reports, variance analyses and commentaries for management review and stakeholder discussion; assist in budgeting, resource planning and financial projections of the University and /or any School, centre, and administrative unit; support the implementation and enhancement of finance systems, including budgeting, planning and reporting modules, and help users adopt related processes and tools effectively; liaise with internal and external auditors, tax advisors and any relevant stakeholders; and implement and promote internal control policies and procedures in accordance with University policy and guidelines. Applicants Should be a qualified accountant with a recognised bachelor’s degree in Finance , Accounting, Business Administration or related disciplines; have at least 8 years of relevant experience in finance and accounting, preferably in the tertiary education sector or Big 4 accounting firms, with solid exposure to business partnering, financial planning and analysis, management reporting, and budgeting; demonstrate strong business acumen and the ability to engage effectively with academic and administrative units, understand their operational priorities and provide practical financial advice; possess strong analytical, financial modelling and problem-solving skills, with the ability to present financial information clearly to non-finance stakeholders; be a proactive team player who can handle duties under tight deadlines, manage multiple priorities and respond effectively to ad hoc requests; demonstrate strong attention to detail, integrity, professionalism and a service-oriented mindset; possess strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trust and work collaboratively with stakeholders at different levels; and be proficient in both written and spoken English and Chinese. Knowledge of Oracle Fusion would be an advantage. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 27 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3867": {
      "title": "Library - Library Assistant I/ Library Assistant II (Collections and Technical Services)",
      "description": "Library - Library Assistant I/ Library Assistant II (Collections and Technical Services) About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 9,900 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Library - Library Assistant I/ Library Assistant II (Collections and Technical Services) (Ref: LA(LIB) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities a ssist in the acquisitions of e-resources and other library materials; m anage license issues, update records in ALMA library management system and troubleshoot the access issues; c ollect data, and analyze usage statistics, and prepare reports for the e-resources management; l iaise with faculties and vendors, in relation to setting up trials, acquisitions, and training; a ssist in collection development activities; c ontribute to library-wide events and activities; and p erform shift duties at service counters. Applicants Should hold a recogni s ed bachelor’s degree or equivalent; have relevant experience preferably in library materials acquisitions, access management, or managing e-resources life cycle and related library systems; possess a solid IT background, with programming skills, and AI literacy being an advantage; exhibit good communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills with the ability to manage complex tasks at a high level of accuracy; and demonstrate positive customer care attitudes and be self-motivated to work independently. The appointee will be required to work shifts in the evenings, on weekends and public holidays. W ork experience in the higher education sector will be an advantage. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 27 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3862": {
      "title": "School of Business",
      "description": "School of Business - Senior Executive Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 7,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures young talent with critical thinking, innovative minds, caring attitudes, moral values and social responsibility. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education, top-quality faculty members, award-winning green campus facilities, innovative degree programmes, a unique residential college system that combines living and learning, interactive small-class teaching, close student-teacher relationships, impactful research, and excellent student development and support services. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place in China. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among China’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : School of Business - Senior Executive Officer (Ref: SEO (SBUS) 2026-09-04) Responsibilities provide support for the postgraduate programme, including student admissions, programme administration, and administrative and secretarial support; serve as a key contact point for students, handle enquiries, and provide timely academic and administrative support throughout their studies; coordinate and liaise with internal departments, external partners, academic staff, and other stakeholders on programme-related matters; plan, coordinate and provide support for programme events, student activities, promotional activities and other programme-related functions; assist in programme promotion, recruitment and student engagement activities as required; maintain programme records, documentation and other administrative information in an accurate and systematic manner; and o ccasionally travel to Chinese Mainland for programme-related activities. Applicants Should possess a bachelor’s degree with at least 5 years of relevant work experience, preferably in tertiary education or academic programme administration; have experience in student admissions, programme administration, event management; be proficient in common office software applications and willing to learn new administrative systems; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua); possess strong communication, organisation, problem-solving and interpersonal skills; and be attentive to details, self-motivated and able to work independently as well as in a team. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 20 September 202 6 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3865": {
      "title": "School of Translation and Foreign Languages - Executive Officer / Assistant Officer",
      "description": "School of Translation and Foreign Languages - Executive Officer / Assistant Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 9,900 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : School of Translation and Foreign Languages - Executive Officer / Assistant Officer (Ref: EO/AO (STFL) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities assist in providing a wide spectrum of support to the School and its academic programmes; liaise with other units, assist in programme administration and admission exercises; organise events such as seminars and exhibitions, and design promotion materials including pamphlets, social media posts; and provide secretarial service to various committees of the School . Applicants Should possess a b achelor’s degree with at least 3 years of working experience, preferably in the education sector; have excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua); have good organisational and communication skills, the ability to work independently, and be proficient in computer skills; and be a team player, responsible, meticulous and self-motivated. Applicants with less experience will be considered as Assistant Officer. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 27 September 2026 .  The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3870": {
      "title": "學生事務處",
      "description": "學生事務處 - 體育助理 關於大學 香港恒生大學是一所以博雅教育為主導的非牟利私立大學，設有六個學院，包括商學院、傳播學院、決策科學學院、人文社會科學學院、翻譯及外語學院和跨學科學院，全日制本科生和研究生逾9,900 人。恒生大學採用獨特的「博雅＋專業」教育模式，致力培育具關懷精神、具備全球視野及負責任領導力的專業人才。 恒生大學矢志成為區內具領導地位的私立大學，致力提供卓越的本科教育和研究導向的研究生教育，並以優質的學生學習體驗、具影響力的研究成果及富意義的社會參與，促進大學向前發展。大學積極推動區域聯繫及國際夥伴關係，為學生和學者營造富有成效的學習與研究環境，鼓勵他們以創新思維和跨學科視野，發揮創意，追求卓越。 恒生大學獲得多項國際認可。在 AppliedHE 公布的2026 年「全亞洲私立大學排名」中，恒生大學位列兩岸四地第七。此外，大學在國際學術平台Research.com的2026年頂尖大學和頂尖科學家排名中，商業與管理領域及經濟與金融領域排名第23、社會科學與人文領域在中國頂尖大學中排名第24位。決策科學學院環球供應鏈管理理學碩士課程，於QS國際貿易碩士課程排名2025中位列世界第84位，而在香港及兩岸四地分別排名第四位及第七位。商學院於2023年獲國際商學院促進協會（AACSB）頒授國際專業認證，成為全球頂尖6%的商學院。恒生大學亦在英國泰晤士高等教育「大學影響力排名 2021」位列「優質教育」及「良好工作和經濟增長」全球首 200 名。 恒大誠邀有興趣人士應徵下列職位空缺： 學生事務處 - 體育助理 (Ref: PEA(SAO) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities 協助管理及巡查校內體育設施，確保設施安全及正常運作； 於服務櫃檯及健身室當值，為使用者提供支援及查詢服務； 協助場地預約、器材借用及收費程序； 協助體育活動、比賽、興趣班及大型活動的場地設置及現場支援； 協助整理及點算體育器材，保持場地整潔； 及 協助處理簡單文書及行政工作。 Applicants Should 持有中學文憑或以上的同等學歷； 熟悉微軟視窗軟件操作，包括文書處理、電子試算表、簡報演示等 ; 懂流利廣東話及基本英語、普通話； 具良好溝通及客戶服務技巧； 對運動及康體設施管理工作有興趣； 工作態度積極主動、具責任感及團隊合作精神； 及 能獨立處理工作及應付突發情況。 如持有急救證書、體適能或運動相關資格者將獲優先考慮。獲聘者需每星期輪班工作五天，包括週一至週五晚上、週六至週日及公眾假期。 .................................................................................................................................................................. 應徵者請於 2026 年 9 月 27 日 或以前透過網上系統 ( https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ ) 登入並遞交 網上 申請。如應徵者於三個月內仍未接獲面試通知，可視作是次申請不被接納。本大學保留不填補此職位的權利。 所有收集的申請及資料只會用作招聘用途，並絕對保密。個人資料收集聲明將按要求提供。 香港恒生大學是一間於香港註冊成立之擔保有限公司 ，為 平等機會僱主。 Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3869": {
      "title": "學生事務處",
      "description": "學生事務處 - 兼職體育助理 關於大學 香港恒生大學是一所以博雅教育為主導的非牟利私立大學，設有六個學院，包括商學院、傳播學院、決策科學學院、人文社會科學學院、翻譯及外語學院和跨學科學院，全日制本科生和研究生逾9,900 人。恒生大學採用獨特的「博雅＋專業」教育模式，致力培育具關懷精神、具備全球視野及負責任領導力的專業人才。 恒生大學矢志成為區內具領導地位的私立大學，致力提供卓越的本科教育和研究導向的研究生教育，並以優質的學生學習體驗、具影響力的研究成果及富意義的社會參與，促進大學向前發展。大學積極推動區域聯繫及國際夥伴關係，為學生和學者營造富有成效的學習與研究環境，鼓勵他們以創新思維和跨學科視野，發揮創意，追求卓越。 恒生大學獲得多項國際認可。在 AppliedHE 公布的2026 年「全亞洲私立大學排名」中，恒生大學位列兩岸四地第七。此外，大學在國際學術平台Research.com的2026年頂尖大學和頂尖科學家排名中，商業與管理領域及經濟與金融領域排名第23、社會科學與人文領域在中國頂尖大學中排名第24位。決策科學學院環球供應鏈管理理學碩士課程，於QS國際貿易碩士課程排名2025中位列世界第84位，而在香港及兩岸四地分別排名第四位及第七位。商學院於2023年獲國際商學院促進協會（AACSB）頒授國際專業認證，成為全球頂尖6%的商學院。恒生大學亦在英國泰晤士高等教育「大學影響力排名 2021」位列「優質教育」及「良好工作和經濟增長」全球首 200 名。 恒大誠邀有興趣人士應徵下列職位空缺： 學生事務處 - 兼職體育助理 (Ref: PTPEA(SAO) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities 協助管理及巡查校內體育設施，確保設施安全及正常運作； 於服務櫃檯及健身室當值，為使用者提供支援及查詢服務； 協助場地預約、器材借用及收費程序； 協助體育活動、比賽、興趣班及大型活動的場地設置及現場支援； 協助整理及點算體育器材，保持場地整潔； 及 協助處理簡單文書及行政工作。 Applicants Should 持有中學文憑或以上的同等學歷； 熟悉微軟視窗軟件操作，包括文書處理、電子試算表、簡報演示等 ; 懂流利廣東話及基本英語、普通話； 具良好溝通及客戶服務技巧； 對運動及康體設施管理工作有興趣； 工作態度積極主動、具責任感及團隊合作精神； 及 能獨立處理工作及應付突發情況。 獲聘者每週工作不多於 16 小時。如持有急救證書、體適能或運動相關資格者，以及可於週一至週五晚上、週六至週日及公眾假期上班將獲優先考慮。 .................................................................................................................................................................. 應徵者請於 2026 年 9 月 27 日 或以前透過網上系統 ( https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ ) 登入並遞交 網上 申請。如應徵者於三個月內仍未接獲面試通知，可視作是次申請不被接納。本大學保留不填補此職位的權利。 所有收集的申請及資料只會用作招聘用途，並絕對保密。個人資料收集聲明將按要求提供。 香港恒生大學是一間於香港註冊成立之擔保有限公司 ，為 平等機會僱主。 Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3864": {
      "title": "Project Officer",
      "description": "Project Officer – Centre for Innovation and Entrepreneurship About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 9,900 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Project Officer – Centre for Innovation and Entrepreneurship (Ref: PO (CIE-830008) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities i mplement and coordinate an ongoing funded project related to youth entrepreneurship in the Greater Bay Area (GBA); l iaise with external and internal stakeholders, including alumni and students, for the effective execution of activities related to this project; m anage the project's budget; p repare promotional materials for the project, including website and social media management; and s erve as secretary in committees and work group s. Applicants Should p ossess a bachelor's degree with at least 3 years of work experience, preferably in the higher education sector or in sizable organisations; h ave a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua); have strong computer skills including MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Chinese word-processing ; d emonstrate excellent interpersonal, organisational, and problem-solving skills ; h ave a strong sense of responsibility and commitment and b e capable of multitasking and attentive to details; be able to w ork independently while being an effective team player; and b e willing to work non-office hours and undertake occasional out-of-town trips. Experience with design software such as Canva, and familiarity with the start-up ecosystem in the Greater Bay Area (GBA), e.g. incubators, accelerators, and entrepreneurship support organisations will be an advantage. Applicants with less work experience will be considered as Assistant Project Officer. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicants should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 20 September 202 6 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3871": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Research Associate – Department of Supply Chain and Information Management About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 9,900 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites application for the Research Project “ AI-Driven Integration of Operations and Security in Smart Warehouses ”, funded by the Research Matching Grant Scheme: Research Associate – Department of Supply Chain and Information Management (Ref: RAsso (SCM – RMGS#840023) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities conduct Supply Chain Management-related project, including model development and organization of research activities; and assist in project management, data collection and analysis, model development and publication work. Applicants Should possess a recognised master’s degree, preferably in Supply Chain Management, Mathematics, Data Science, Engineering or other related discipline, with at least 3 years of work experience in Supply Chain Management research and project management; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; have good interpersonal and communication skills; and be organised, self-motivated, a good team player, and able to work independently with a strong sense of responsibility. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 20 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3866": {
      "title": "Research Associate / Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Associate / Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant – Department of Computer Science About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and over 9,900 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the Project “Quantifying Privacy Risk of Mobile Applications with the Help of GenAI - An Empirical Study”, funded by the School Research Grants: Research Associate / Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant – Department of Computer Science (Ref: RAsso / SRA / RA (COM - SDSC – SRG073) 2026-09-11) Responsibilities use Machine Learning, Large Language Models in particular, to understand the relationship between descriptions and permissions of mobile applications; perform data analysis; and assist in documentation. Applicants Should Research Associate: possess a master’s degree or above in Computer Science, Information Technology , or a related discipline, with at least 3 years of work experience in research or industry practice; Senior Research Assistant: possess a bachelor’s degree or above in Computer Science, Information Technology , or a related discipline, with at least 3 years of work experience in research or industry practice; Research Assistant: possess a bachelor’s degree or above in Computer Science, Information Technology , or a related discipline possess good programming skills in Python; have a good understanding of Machine Learning and/or Deep Learning will be an advantage; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; and have the ability to work independently and under pressure. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 27 September 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    }
